<?xml version="1.0" encoding="utf-8"?>
<odoo>

<!--
    "Nos Actualités": the three latest published blog posts.

    Read live from blog.post at the moment the block is DROPPED, exactly like
    the category tiles — dragging a snippet inserts the rendered html, so the
    page stores plain cards and the client can edit them like any other block.
    models/tecas_autosync.py re-renders every copy marked data-tecas-auto="1"
    whenever a post is written, published or removed, so the homepage follows
    the blog without anyone touching the page.

    NEVER copy this template's source into a page arch: a t-* attribute under
    #wrap costs the page every editor drop zone. See s_tecas_categories.xml.

    Pictures come from _tecas_cover_url() — the post's cover if it has one,
    otherwise the first image in its body. Posts with neither get the block's
    own placeholder rather than website_blog's stock cover_5.jpg, which is a
    photo of somebody else's product. Setting a cover on the post (Blog → the
    post → Modifier → Couverture) is what puts a real picture here.

    Titles are printed with t-out, not t-field: they must not become editable
    in the page editor, or editing the page would rewrite the posts themselves.
-->
<template id="s_tecas_news" name="Nos actualités">
    <section class="s_tecas_news pt64 pb64" data-tecas-auto="1">
        <div class="container">
            <h2 class="s_tecas_lead_title text-center">Nos Actualités</h2>

            <t t-set="tecas_posts" t-value="env['blog.post'].sudo()._tecas_latest_posts(3)"/>
            <div class="row g-4">
                <div t-foreach="tecas_posts" t-as="post" class="col-12 col-md-6 col-lg-4">
                    <a t-att-href="post.website_url" class="s_tecas_news_card">
                        <span class="s_tecas_news_img">
                            <t t-set="cover" t-value="post._tecas_cover_url()"/>
                            <img t-att-src="cover or '/tecas_website_blocks/static/src/img/s_tecas_news_photo.svg'"
                                 t-att-alt="post.name" loading="lazy"/>
                        </span>
                        <span class="s_tecas_news_body">
                            <span class="s_tecas_news_title" t-out="post.name"/>
                            <span class="s_tecas_news_link">Continuer la lecture</span>
                        </span>
                    </a>
                </div>
            </div>

            <div class="s_tecas_cta s_tecas_cta_center">
                <a href="/blog" class="s_tecas_cta_btn s_tecas_cta_btn_quote">
                    Voir toutes les actualités
                </a>
            </div>
        </div>
    </section>
</template>

</odoo>
